# Superseded by the Parquet warehouse: listings.jsonl is 10MB and rebuilds from
# etl/raw, while fact_listing.parquet holds the same rows in 488KB. Committing
# both would burn the git headroom the warehouse design depends on.
data/market/listings.jsonl
data/market/listings.csv

# Cached Wikipedia and vendor prose for the care backfill. Regenerates from
# `npm run care:fetch`, and it is the article text itself - several megabytes
# that churn on every Wikipedia edit. The derived records beside it
# (fetch-log.json, care-proposals.jsonl, care-review.jsonl) ARE committed,
# because those are the audit trail.
data/care/text/

# Emitted by a stray "tsc --noEmit false"; these shadow the .ts sources at runtime.
src/**/*.js
etl/**/*.js
/vite.config.js
/vitest.config.js

# Agent/tooling scratch, not part of the app.
.playwright-mcp/
.remember/
.tmp/

# Git worktrees live here so concurrent sessions stop switching each other's
# branches. They are whole checkouts of this repo - committing one would nest
# the repository inside itself. .claude/skills/ IS tracked, deliberately.
.claude/worktrees/

# Dexie Cloud CLI state. `dexie-cloud.key` holds a client secret that can
# administer the database - delete tables, read every realm - so it must never
# reach this public repo (NFR-10).
#
# `dexie-cloud.json` was deliberately left tracked when there was one database,
# on the reasoning that its URL is public and committing it tells a fresh
# checkout where to sync. That reasoning expired. There are now three databases
# (scratch, uat, production), the URL a build should use is committed source in
# `src/data/environment.ts` where it is chosen per deployment and tested, and
# `npx dexie-cloud connect` REWRITES this file every time you switch. Tracked,
# it would sit permanently dirty and one careless `git add -A` would point
# production at scratch. It is machine state, not configuration.
dexie-cloud.key
dexie-cloud.json

